[comment {-*- mode: tcl ; fill-column: 90 -*- doctools manpage}]
[vset VERSION 0.15.5]
[manpage_begin mndoc n [vset VERSION]]
[copyright {2019-2026, Detlef Groth <detlef(at)uni(minus)potsdam(dot)de>}]
[moddesc   {Source code documentation using Markdown}]
[titledesc {Source code documentation extractor/converter application}]
[category  {Text processing}]
[description]

This document describes [cmd mndoc], an application to extract documentation embedded in
source code files, be they [file .tcl], or other, and to convert Markdown files to HTML.


[section {Command Line}]

[list_begin definitions]

[call [cmd mndoc] [option --help]]

The application prints a short help to standard output and exits.

[call [cmd mndoc] [option --version]]

The application prints its version number to standard output and exits.

[call [cmd mndoc] [option --license]]

The application prints its license to standard output and exits.

[call [cmd mndoc] [arg input] [arg output] [arg options]]

The application reads the [arg input] file, extracts the embedded documentation, and
writes it to the [arg output] file.

[para] If the output file is not a [file .md] file the extracted documentation is
converted to HTML before being written.

[para] If both [arg input] and [arg output] are HTML files, the application only
embeds local images and stylesheets as base64 data into a standalone HTML file.

[para] When generating and writing HTML the default CSS stylesheet can be overridden by
specifying the path to a custom stylesheet via option [option --css]. If the
--css file name is either [file mndoc.css] or [file tmdoc.css] and if it does not
yet exist in the folder, then the file is copied from the package folder into
the current folder.

[para] If the input file is a [file .md] file it is expected to contain Markdown as-is,
instead of Markdown embedded into code.

[para] On the other side, when the file is considered code then the documentation is
expected to be contained in all lines starting with the marker [const "#'"].

For script languages like Tcl the [const #] character of this marker means that the
documentation is contained in the so-flagged comments.

For other languages the marker and documentation may have to be embedded into multi-line
comments.

[list_end]

[section Options]

[list_begin definitions]

[call [option --base64] [arg boolean]]

Embed local images and CSS files as base64 data. The default is [const true].
JavaScript files are not embedded. When both the input and output files are HTML,
this option controls whether the assets are inlined.

[call [option --bodyonly] [arg boolean]]

Write only the content of the HTML body, omitting the HTML header and footer. The
default is [const false].

[call [option --css] [arg cssfile[,cssfile...]]]

Use the given stylesheet or stylesheets instead of the built-in default
stylesheet. Multiple files can be separated by commas.

[call [option --footer] [arg footer.html]]

Insert the given HTML file before the closing [const body] tag of an HTML output
file.

[call [option --header] [arg header.html]]

Insert the given HTML file after the opening [const body] tag of an HTML output
file.

[call [option --javascript] [arg highlightjs|file1.js,file2.js]]

Embed the highlight.js highlighter or the given local JavaScript files into an
HTML output file. Multiple local files can be separated by commas.

[call [option --mathjax] [arg boolean]]

Include the MathJax JavaScript library so that embedded LaTeX formulas are
rendered. The default is [const false].

[call [option --refresh] [arg seconds]]

Add an automatic refresh header to an HTML output file. Values of 10 or above
are considered. The default is [const 0], which disables refreshing.

[list_end]

[section Examples]

[example {
    # Create HTML manual for a CPP file using a custom style sheet
    mndoc sample.cpp sample.html --css manual.css

    # Create HTML manual for a Python file using the package mndoc.css file
    mndoc sample.py sample.html --css mndoc.css

    # Extract the documentation from code as simple Markdown, ready to be processed
    # further, for example with pandoc, or similar
    mndoc sample.cpp sample.md 

    # Convert a Markdown file to HTML
    mndoc sample.md sample.html

    # Convert a Markdown file to HTML with syntax highlighting
    mndoc sample.md sample.html --javascript highlightjs

    # Convert a Markdown file to HTML and render LaTeX formulas
    mndoc sample.md sample.html --mathjax true

    # Embed images and stylesheet files into an existing HTML file
    mndoc sample.html sample-out.html
}]

